# Files a linked worktree receives that git would otherwise leave behind.
#
# Gitignore syntax. Only untracked-AND-ignored paths are eligible: anything tracked
# already travels with the checkout, so naming it here would be inert. The transfer is
# a copy taken once at creation — a snapshot, not a live share.
#
# The rule: project DATA travels, the ledger does not. A second working copy reads the
# project sheet, the product context, the domain rules and the task artifacts it needs
# to work; the backlog, the session state, the decision log, the archive and the icebox
# bodies stay with the primary checkout, which remains their single writer.
#
# The icebox is named here because it is the one that looks like data and is not: its
# index lives in the backlog, its identifiers are minted in the coordinator, and a front
# that needs an entry reads it there read-only. Where this directory is ignored, leaving
# the icebox unlisted is what keeps it out. Where the project commits it, git carried it
# in with the checkout and no pattern file can select against that — there what protects
# it is the written rule that a front never writes the ledger, not this file.
#
# The engine itself is deliberately absent: protocols, skills, hooks and the runner live
# in ~/.claude and reach every worktree without being copied.
.ai-flow/project.yml
.ai-flow/product.md
.ai-flow/steering/
.ai-flow/artifacts/
